From 62d2fe64c270fa198c732692c6347527939184de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:46:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Netplay: survive a peer leaving, size the buffer from ping,
 and keep teams private

Four release blockers, one commit.

Session loss. A peer that vanished used to leave everyone else waiting on an
unbounded event with crit_netplay_client held, so closing the Android app froze
the desktop side until ENet gave up 30s later -- and often not even then. The
wait is now bounded and re-checked, and a session only ends when something
corroborates that the peer is really gone: the pad's owner has left the room,
or the socket has been silent for 20s. A peer that merely paused or backgrounded
never ends anyone's session. Ordinary stops stay silent; only genuine losses say
so. Android also announces its own departure through a task watcher, so a swipe
away is a clean goodbye rather than a timeout.

Buffer. The host now sizes the input buffer from measured ping --
ceil(ping / 16.67) + 2 frames, clamped to [3, 20] -- raising quickly when the
link degrades and lowering one frame at a time only after 30 quiet samples, so
it cannot oscillate. Editing the buffer by hand turns the sizer off for the rest
of the session.

Trainer name. The team editor can set the in-game name, and a netplay submission
carries it alongside the team, so a guest playing in someone else's room shows
up under their own name instead of the host's. The payload stays one string and
both directions interoperate with older clients.

Team privacy. A Gen 3 save carries every EV, IV and nature, so a leftover copy
is a scouting tool. End-of-session cleanup now also takes the .bak, .tmp and
marker files and netplay's NetPlayTemp staging saves, and -- because the live
mGBA core rewrites the save during teardown -- it waits for emulation to reach
Uninitialized before doing any of it. The desktop guest-slot lock is now scoped
to the room rather than to the running game, which is when submissions actually
arrive.
